    "body": "- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\nHello from nvim-tree\r\n\r\n`NvimTreeGitDirty` was linking to itself. Used 0E as per gitsigns.\r\n\r\nUpdated `NvimTreeGitNew` from 0D to 0A as per neo-tree for better legibility.",
    "closed_at": "2022-12-25T08:11:43Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks! I didn't think linking to itself is even possible... I think it was meant to be linked to `NvimTreeGitDeleted` as per ['nvim-tree' default colors](https://github.com/nvim-tree/nvim-tree.lua/blob/9e4c39572f631bb60ee15cb9d46e1daa9927a45e/lua/nvim-tree/colors.lua#L44-L45). But I like your second reasoning more: making it more aligned with 'neo-tree' seems like a better choice. In 'nvim-tree' `NvimTreeGitDirty` is used for unstaged files, so will make it aligned with `NeoTreeGitUnstaged`, i.e. `base08` (which also the same for `NvimTreeGitDeleted`).\r\n\r\nChange of `NvimTreeGitNew` to `base0A` is also good.\r\n\r\nI'll merge in separate branch and make joint commit. Thanks for PR!\r\n",
            "created_at": "2022-12-25T08:11:07Z",
